  "market_context": "EUR/USD on the 15-minute chart with the Asia session range marked between approximately 1.11580 and 1.11680. London session opens and begins probing both sides of the Asia range without sustained direction, setting up a Seek and Destroy daily profile.",
  "key_observation": "London sweeps outside the Asia range then aggressively reverses back inside, then fails to displace on the opposite side as well. With no directional commitment, price oscillates back to equilibrium and the daily open, forming an indecision candle on the daily.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Mark out the Asia session high and low on the 15-minute EUR/USD chart to define the initial range.",
    "Step 2: Observe London push outside the Asia range and then aggressively snap back inside, signaling no directional commitment on that side.",
    "Step 3: Watch price travel to the opposite side of the Asia range and again fail to displace or break out cleanly.",
    "Step 4: With both sides swept and rejected, mark discount and premium of the range and target equilibrium plus the daily open as draws on price.",
    "Step 5: Extend the levels forward; as price makes a new low, track discount/premium of the new leg and again expect a return into the original range and toward the daily open.",
    "Step 6: Confirm the day closes as an indecision candle on the daily timeframe, validating the Seek and Destroy profile."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Seek and Destroy days are not for participation but for recognition. When London takes both sides of the Asia range without displacement, expect oscillation back to equilibrium and the daily open. The proper response is to stay out of the market.",
